---
import { experience } from '../data/experience';
import { site } from '../data/site';
import SectionHead from './SectionHead.astro';

const current = experience[0];
---

<section class="section about" aria-labelledby="story-title">
  <div class="container">
    <SectionHead id="story-title" title="The short version" />

    <div class="grid-12 story">
      <dl class="facts mono" data-reveal>
        <div><dt>Based in</dt><dd>{site.location}</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Building since</dt><dd>2018</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Now</dt><dd>{current ? `${current.role}, ${current.organisation}` : site.role}</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Recognition</dt><dd>1st place, Devday Hackathon 2021</dd></div>
      </dl>

      <div class="prose copy" data-reveal>
        <p>
          I’ve been building for the web since 2018. The work that stuck with me was always about the reasoning: why this screen, why this stack, why now.
        </p>
        <p>
          Design work taught me to frame a problem for the people who have it. Frontend and full-stack work taught me what each decision costs to build. Managing delivery on SEAN-CSO taught me that most problems live between management and developers.
        </p>
        <p>
          Today I lead technical delivery across web, mobile, and computer-vision work at Nusapala Berkah Autonomous, after project-engineering and UI/UX roles at ABAROBOTICS.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .facts { grid-column: 1 / span 3; display: grid; gap: 1.25rem; align-content: start; }
  .facts div { border-top: var(--hairline); padding-top: 0.75rem; }
  .facts dt { color: var(--muted); }
  .facts dd { margin-top: 0.25rem; color: var(--text-2); }
  .copy { grid-column: 4 / span 8; font-size: var(--step-1); color: var(--text-2); }
  .copy p { color: var(--text-2); }
  .copy p:first-child { color: var(--text); }

  /* LAYOUT_BREAKPOINT — see src/constants.ts */
  @media (max-width: 900px) {
    .story { display: flex; flex-direction: column-reverse; gap: 2.5rem; }
  }
</style>
